# The API image needs the Python package (etl/, data/, scripts/), its lockfile
# and Alembic. Everything else is either a secret, a local environment, or a
# different deployable: the website ships to Vercel on its own.
#
# NOTE: `data/` here is the SQLAlchemy package (session, models, migrations),
# not a data directory. It must stay in the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
**/__pycache__/
*.log
website/
tests/
project-management/
docker-compose.yml
